US, is there a brand already existing in your country or some of like a TV show that has the same name that we should be aware of? And you can't underestimate the importance of linguistic checks once they were naming a little gadget toy. And one of the names that we had come up with for them turned out in Japanese to be a word that meant a small device that doesn't work. So we took that one right off the list. But more than anything else, Laurel and her team at Catchword just produce a ton of names.
美国之外，你的国家是否已经存在一个品牌，或者是否有我们应该注意的同名电视节目？你不能低估语言检查的重要性。有一次他们正在为一个小玩具命名。我们为他们想出的名字之一，在日语中竟然是一个意思为“无法工作的小装置”的词。所以我们立刻把它从名单上删除了。但最重要的是，Laurel和她在Catchword的团队确实产出了大量的名字。

