00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:38.000
because they come up with names across the naming spectrum. Okay, so we always draw a spectrum because we're talking about language, it's always a spectrum. So at one end of the spectrum, you have descriptive names. And those are names that absolutely just describe what the thing is. Classic example. Raising brand.
是因为他们是在整个命名范围内进行构思。好吧，我们总是画一个光谱，因为我们在谈论语言，它总是一个光谱。在光谱的一端，你有描述性名称。这些名字绝对只是描述了事物本身。经典的例子：葡萄干麦麸（Raisin Bran）。

11
00:04:38.000 --> 00:05:01.000
Benefits of descriptive names. They are self-explanatory. That's what that stuff is, right? It's a box. It's brand and it has raisins in it. You would never have to. That's what that stuff is, right? It's a box, it's brand, and it has raisins in it. You would never have to explain to anybody what this stuff is. Shredded wheat. That's what that is. It's wheat, and it's been shredded. Drawbacks to descriptive names, they are hard to own. Normally, you can't trademark names like this. In fact, raisened brand and shredded wheat are not trademarks.
描述性名称的好处是：它们是不言自明的。这就是那东西，对吧？它是一个盒子。它是麦麸，里面有葡萄干。你永远不需要向任何人解释这东西是什么。碎麦片（Shredded Wheat）。这就是它。它是小麦，而且被切碎了。描述性名称的缺点是：它们很难拥有。通常，你不能为这样的名字注册商标。事实上，Raisin Bran和Shredded Wheat都不是商标。

12
00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:30.000
Anybody can have a cereal and call it raisened brand or shredded wheat. So a lot of descriptive names tend to get modified. International business machines. Frity darn descriptive. Over time they've condensed that to IBM. The other big drawback is that descriptive names can be limited. If you remember there were companies called things like e-stamps, right? If you ever want to do anything but sell electronic stamps you're screwed. On the other end of the spectrum you've got so-called arbitrary names. And Apple is a great example of that.
任何人都可以生产一种麦片并称之为Raisin Bran或Shredded Wheat。所以很多描述性名称往往会被修改。国际商业机器公司（International Business Machines）。非常该死的描述性。随着时间的推移，他们将其缩写为IBM。另一个大缺点是描述性名称可能会受到限制。如果你还记得，曾经有一些公司叫“e-stamps”之类的名字，对吧？如果你以后想做除了卖电子邮票以外的任何事情，你就完蛋了。在光谱的另一端，你有所谓的任意名称。苹果（Apple）就是一个很好的例子。

13
00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:58.000
It doesn't tell you anything about what they do, which allows for flexibility. They used to just make computers. Now they do media. They could do anything under that. I mean, they could make cars. But Apple is a real word that you can find in the dictionary, of course. It is its own set of associations. Maybe Apple implies learning or freshness, I don't know. But it doesn't apply to the thing, it's naming. Arbitrary names can also just be completely made up.
它没有告诉你任何关于他们做什么的信息，这提供了灵活性。他们过去只制造电脑。现在他们做媒体。他们可以在此名下做任何事情。我的意思是，他们甚至可以制造汽车。但Apple当然是一个可以在字典里找到的真实单词。它有自己的一套联想。也许Apple暗示了学习或新鲜感，我不知道。但它并不适用于产品本身，这就是命名。任意名称也可以是完全编造出来的。

