It mostly comes down to what kind of story, if any, you want behind your name. Some clients really want a meaningless name. Remember, made-up names are easier to register domains or trademarks for and are less likely to offend. And if it's a meaningless word, if it's just a completely coined made-up word, you can make up any story you want around it. A name like Hulu, for example. As far as I know, it doesn't actually have any real meaning. I know that Hulu, the inventors of that, have a story around that name.
这主要归结为你想要名字背后有什么样的故事（如果有的话）。有些客户确实想要一个毫无意义的名字。记住，编造的名字更容易注册域名或商标，也不太可能冒犯他人。如果它是一个毫无意义的词，如果它只是一个完全编造的合成词，你可以在它周围编造任何你想要的故事。比如Hulu这个名字。据我所知，它实际上没有任何真正的含义。我知道Hulu的创始人围绕那个名字编了一个故事。

